      "attestations": [
        {
          "text": "CHU Chih-yü 朱之瑜 (T. 魯嶼, 楚嶼, H. 舜水), Nov. 17, 1600–1682, May 23, was a native of Yü-yao, Chekiang. Both his father and grandfather were Ming officials, and he himself repeatedly declined invitations to accept high positions under the Manchus until his loyalty was questioned and he was forced in 1645 to flee to Japan.",
          "source": "eccp-3636411",
